1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,220
A legal one percent fee robbed you of three hundred sixteen grand.

2
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:05,840
Here's how that shit works.

3
00:00:06,360 --> 00:00:11,720
You put in five hundred bucks a month for forty years. That's two hundred forty grand of your own money.

4
00:00:12,220 --> 00:00:15,460
Assume it grows seven percent a year. Just an assumption, calm down.

5
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:20,520
Picture two identical funds, except one charges a one percent fee every year.

6
00:00:20,960 --> 00:00:23,300
Double-tap if you've literally never looked at yours.

7
00:00:23,900 --> 00:00:28,100
A fee is the cut they keep for managing your money. That sounds pretty harmless, right?

8
00:00:28,100 --> 00:00:32,760
After ten years, you're down about forty-six hundred. Whatever, who cares, right?

9
00:00:33,180 --> 00:00:35,760
Send this to whoever thinks one percent is nothing.

10
00:00:36,480 --> 00:00:38,240
Wait until thirty years: over a hundred thousand.

11
00:00:39,900 --> 00:00:45,540
And why is that? The fee takes one percent of your whole damn pile, every year, growth included.

12
00:00:46,300 --> 00:00:49,700
Forty years later, the no-fee fund has about one point three million.

13
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:52,260
Follow, 'cause this next number hurts.

14
00:00:52,840 --> 00:00:54,400
The one percent fund? About nine hundred ninety-six thousand.

15
00:00:56,240 --> 00:01:01,200
So that tiny fee took three hundred sixteen grand, more than you ever put in.

16
00:01:01,580 --> 00:01:05,200
That's most of a house, gone, for a fee you never even noticed.

17
00:01:05,940 --> 00:01:07,340
Still small? One word.

